# Rust Coding Standards for Shem

## Code Style
- Follow Rust standard formatting with `cargo fmt`
- Use `cargo clippy` for linting and best practices
- Prefer `anyhow::Result` for error handling in CLI code
- Use `thiserror` for custom error types in library crates
- Follow async/await patterns consistently

## Error Handling
- Use `anyhow::Result<T>` for CLI commands in [crates/cli/src/](mdc:crates/cli/src/)
- Use `thiserror` for structured errors in library crates
- Always provide meaningful error messages
- Use `?` operator for error propagation

## Testing
- Write unit tests in `mod tests` blocks within source files
- Use `#[cfg(test)]` for test-only modules
- Integration tests go in [crates/*/tests/](mdc:crates/*/tests/) directories
- Use `test-log` crate for logging in tests
- Use `tempfile` for temporary database testing

## Dependencies
- Check [Cargo.toml](mdc:Cargo.toml) for workspace dependencies
- Use workspace dependencies when possible
- Keep dependencies minimal and up-to-date
- Use `cargo upgrade` to update dependencies

## Async Patterns
- Use `tokio` runtime for async operations
- Prefer `async fn` for database operations
- Use `async-trait` for trait methods that need to be async
- Handle async operations properly in CLI commands

## Documentation
- Use `///` for public API documentation
- Include examples in doc comments
- Document error conditions and edge cases
- Keep README files updated with usage examples
